basic guide to work your way around path:

from pathlib import path

then we create an object file:
    1- we can pass anything to this object, literally anything
     - we usually pass paths here, but its better to pass something valid

ex:
    p = path("this/path/does/exist")
    print(p.exists())     # False
    print(p.is_file())    # False
    print(p.is_dir())     # False

==> the path becomes real when we do I/O with it: read, open, mkdir, etc...


